Highlight the filter match in Wigwag's issue titles

filterQuery filters rows (Issue Tracker.dc.html, in the rows builder: issues.filter(i => (i.values.title||'').toLowerCase().includes(q))) but never marks the matched text, so users see the browser's find-in-page block instead. Add our own highlight.

Scope. Title cell only — the only field the filter searches. If the filter is widened to notes/comments later, highlight there too: an unhighlighted hit in a row with no visible match reads as a bug.

Treatment. Wrap each matched run in a span with:

    background: var(--c4) — the pale accent already used around the comment-count badge; works in both token sets, no new tokens
    text colour unchanged (inherits var(--n7)). Do not reverse to white-on-accent — at 13px/600 it reads worse than the plain text either side
    border-radius: 3px
    padding: 1px 0 — no horizontal padding. Any inset makes the fill overhang the glyphs, so a match at the start of a line sits a few px left of every other row's first character and the column's left edge goes ragged
    box-decoration-break: clone + -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone — wigwag-core contains a hyphen so the browser will break it as wigwag- / core; without clone the fragments render as sheared rectangles with square inner corners

Splitting. In renderVals(), where the title cell's displayText is built, emit a parts array when a filter is active — all occurrences, case-insensitive, alternating plain and match:

const splitMatches = (text, q) => {
  if (!q) return [{ text, isPlain: true, isMatch: false }];
  const hay = text.toLowerCase(), needle = q.toLowerCase();
  const parts = [];
  let i = 0;
  while (i < text.length) {
    const at = hay.indexOf(needle, i);
    if (at < 0) { parts.push({ text: text.slice(i), isPlain: true, isMatch: false }); break; }
    if (at > i) parts.push({ text: text.slice(i, at), isPlain: true, isMatch: false });
    parts.push({ text: text.slice(at, at + needle.length), isPlain: false, isMatch: true });
    i = at + needle.length;
  }
  return parts;
};

Mark every occurrence — titles like "Phase 4: build a wigwag CLI on wigwag-core.js" have two, and marking only the first looks arbitrary.

Template. Inside the existing row.title.isPlain span, replace {{ row.title.displayText }} with an sc-for over parts holding two sc-if branches (match → styled span, plain → bare span). Keep the sc-for, both sc-ifs and their spans on one line with no whitespace between tags — source newlines become text nodes and insert spaces mid-word. Keep title="{{ row.title.displayText }}" on the cell so the tooltip stays the plain string.

